Maximum rewind time := historyAmount * captureIntervalÜ¨␀␀␀␀Å∞Capture state every 'captureInterval' seconds. Larger values will space out the captures more, which gives a longer history but with possible gaps inbetween.
Smaller values will have fewer gaps, with shorter history.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀4Event Listeners (optional)␀␀ÄñMirror has an internal subscriber to this event. You can add your own here.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÄñMirror has an internal subscriber to this event. You can add your own here.◊¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Å‹Server Authority calls OnSerialize on the server and syncs it to clients.

Client Authority calls OnSerialize on the owning client, syncs it to server, which then broadcasts it to all other clients.

Use server authority for cheat safety.◊¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ÅtBy default synced data is sent from the server to all Observers of the object.
Change this to Owner to only have the server update the client that has ownership authority for this object◊¨␀␀ä¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀@␀␀ÅÏTime in seconds until next change is synchronized to the client. '0' means send immediately if changed. '0.5' means only send changes every 500ms.
(This is for state synchronization like SyncVars, SyncLists, OnSerialize. Not for Cmds, Rpcs, etc.)ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Ä¸Occasionally send a full reliable state to delta compress against. This only applies to Components with SyncMethod=Unreliable.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÄÙEnable to send all unreliable messages twice. Only useful for extremely fast-paced games since it doubles bandwidth costs.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÅWhen sending a reliable baseline, should we also send an unreliable delta or rely on the reliable baseline to arrive in a similar time?â¨␀␀␀␀
Debugﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀tØ␀␀◊¨␀␀␀␀m_SceneId␀␀␀Ù≠␀␀◊¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀tØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀m_ServerOnly␀␀xPrevents this object from being spawned / enabled on clientsﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀Ü¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀Å∞Visibility can overwrite interest management. ForceHidden can be useful to hide monsters while they respawn. ForceShown can be useful for score NetworkIdentities that should always broadcast to everyone in the world.␀␀visibleﬁ␀␀␀␀␀Ù≠␀␀◊¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀â¨␀␀tØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Configuration␀␀&m_DontDestroyOnLoad␀␀ÄäShould the Network Manager object be persisted through scene changes?tØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀"m_RunInBackground␀␀Ä¨Multiplayer games should always run in the background so the network doesn't time out.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀$Auto-Start Options␀␀ÄàChoose whether Server or Client should auto-start in headless buildsÜ¨␀␀␀␀ÄæHeadless Start Mode in Editor
when enabled, headless start mode will be used in editor as well.Ü¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀ÅºServer / Client send rate per second.
Use 60-100Hz for fast paced games like Counter-Strike to minimize latency.
Use around 30Hz for games like WoW to minimize computations.
Use around 1-10Hz for slow paced games like EVE.␀␀serverTickRatetØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀â¨␀␀u‡␀␀␀␀m_OfflineScene␀␀ÄäScene that Mirror will switch to when the client or server is stopped␀␀ Scene Management␀␀␀u‡␀␀tØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀m_OnlineScene␀␀Å.Scene that Mirror will switch to when the server is started. Clients will recieve a Scene Message to load the server's current scene when they connect.Ü¨␀␀ä¨␀␀␀␀ÅfOptional delay that can be used after disconnecting to show a 'Connection lost...' message or similar before loading the offline scene, which may take a long time in big projects.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀pBâ¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Network Info␀␀Ä¨Transport component attached to this object that server and client will use to connecttØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀ m_NetworkAddress␀␀Ä Network Address where the client should connect to the server. Server does not use this for anything.Ü¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀RMaximum number of concurrent connections.␀␀ m_MaxConnectionsÜ¨␀␀␀␀Ä When enabled, the server automatically disconnects inactive connections after the configured timeout.Ü¨␀␀␀␀Ä˙Timeout in seconds for server to automatically disconnect inactive connections if 'disconnectInactiveConnections' is enabled.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Authentication␀␀`Authentication component attached to this objectâ¨␀␀tØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Player Object␀␀m_PlayerPrefab␀␀ÄÚPrefab of the player object. Prefab must have a Network Identity component. May be an empty game object or a full avatar.Ü¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀ÄÄShould Mirror automatically spawn the player after scene change?␀␀$m_AutoCreatePlayertØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀&m_PlayerSpawnMethod␀␀nRound Robin or Random order of Start Position selectiontØ␀␀◊¨␀␀␀␀m_SpawnPrefabs␀␀␀â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Security␀␀ÇlFor security, it is recommended to disconnect a player if a networked action triggers an exception
This could prevent components being accessed in an undefined state, which may be an attack vector for exploits.
However, some games may want to allow exceptions in order to not interrupt the player's experience.â¨␀␀␀␀,Snapshot Interpolationâ¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀$Connection Quality␀␀ÅMethod to use for connection quality evaluation.
