Pragmatic: based on snapshot interpolation adjustment.Ü¨␀␀ä¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀ÄÃInterval in seconds to evaluate connection quality.
Set to 0 to disable connection quality evaluation.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀pB␀␀2connectionQualityIntervalâ¨␀␀␀␀\Interpolation UI - Requires Editor / Dev Buildﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀ﬁ␀␀␀␀␀Ü¨␀␀â¨␀␀␀␀Å‚Local simulation is behind by sendInterval * multiplier seconds.

This guarantees that we always have enough snapshots in the buffer to mitigate lags & jitter.

Increase this if the simulation isn't smooth. By default, it should be around 2.␀␀BufferingÜ¨␀␀␀␀ÄåIf a client can't process snapshots fast enough, don't store too many.Ü¨␀␀â¨␀␀␀␀ÅêSlowdown begins when the local timeline is moving too fast towards remote time. Threshold is in frames worth of snapshots.

This needs to be negative.

Don't modify unless you know what you are doing.␀␀$Catchup / SlowdownÜ¨␀␀␀␀Å∫Catchup begins when the local timeline is moving too slow and getting too far away from remote time. Threshold is in frames worth of snapshots.

This needs to be positive.

Don't modify unless you know what you are doing.Ü¨␀␀ä¨␀␀␀␀fLocal timeline acceleration in % while catching up.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä?Ü¨␀␀ä¨␀␀␀␀`Local timeline slowdown in % while slowing down.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä?Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÄåCatchup/Slowdown is adjusted over n-second exponential moving average.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀$Dynamic Adjustment␀␀Å0Automatically adjust bufferTimeMultiplier for smooth results.
