Debugä¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀â¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀@F␀␀ÅtLatency in milliseconds (1000 = 1 second). Always applied to both reliable and unreliable, otherwise unreliable NetworkTime may be behind reliable [SyncVars/Commands/Rpcs] or vice versa!␀␀Commonä¨␀␀tØ␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ä?␀␀,latencySpikeMultiplier␀␀lJitter latency via perlin(Time * jitterSpeed) * jitterÜ¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀lJitter latency via perlin(Time * jitterSpeed) * jitter␀␀6latencySpikeSpeedMultiplierÜ¨␀␀ä¨␀␀â¨␀␀â¨␀␀␀␀Å^Packet loss in %
2% recommended for long term play testing, upto 5% for short bursts.
Anything higher, or for a prolonged amount of time, suggests user has a connection fault.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀»B␀␀&Unreliable Messages␀␀"Reliable Messagesä¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀»B␀␀Ä∆Scramble % of unreliable messages, just like over the real network. Mirror unreliable is unordered.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Common␀␀fNagle Algorithm can be disabled by enabling NoDelayÜ¨␀␀␀␀:Send timeout in milliseconds.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÄºReceive timeout in milliseconds. High by default so users don't time out during scene changes.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Server␀␀Å∆Protect against allocation attacks by keeping the max message size small. Otherwise an attacker might send multiple fake packets with 2GB headers, causing the server to run out of memory after allocating multiple large packets.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÅLServer processes a limit amount of messages per tick to avoid a deadlock where it might end up processing forever if messages come in faster than we can process them.Ü¨␀␀␀␀Å®Server send queue limit per connection for pending messages. Telepathy will disconnect a connection's queues reach that limit for load balancing. Better to kick one slow client than slowing down the whole server.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÅÆServer receive queue limit per connection for pending messages. Telepathy will disconnect a connection's queues reach that limit for load balancing. Better to kick one slow client than slowing down the whole server.â¨␀␀Ü¨␀␀␀␀Client␀␀ÅÊProtect against allocation attacks by keeping the max message size small. Otherwise an attacker host might send multiple fake packets with 2GB headers, causing the connected clients to run out of memory after allocating multiple large packets.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÅLClient processes a limit amount of messages per tick to avoid a deadlock where it might end up processing forever if messages come in faster than we can process them.Ü¨␀␀␀␀Å:Client send queue limit for pending messages. Telepathy will disconnect if the connection's queues reach that limit in order to avoid ever growing latencies.Ü¨␀␀␀␀Å@Client receive queue limit for pending messages. Telepathy will disconnect if the connection's queues reach that limit in order to avoid ever growing latencies.Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÅíDetect device sleep mode and automatically disconnect + hibernate the thread after 'sleepTimeout' seconds.
For example: on mobile / VR, we don't want to drain the battery after putting down the device.Ü¨␀␀␀␀Å∆Protect against allocation attacks by keeping the max message size small. Otherwise an attacker might send multiple fake packets with 2GB headers, causing the server to run out of memory after allocating multiple large packets.Ü¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀rMax size for http header send as handshake for websockets␀␀ handshakeMaxSizeÜ¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀ÅfCaps the number of messages the server will process per tick. Allows LateUpdate to finish to let the reset of unity continue in case more messages arrive before they are processed␀␀0serverMaxMessagesPerTickÜ¨␀␀tØ␀␀␀␀ÅfCaps the number of messages the client will process per tick. Allows LateUpdate to finish to let the reset of unity continue in case more messages arrive before they are processed␀␀0clientMaxMessagesPerTickÜ¨␀␀␀␀Ä–Send would stall forever if the network is cut off during a send, so we need a timeout (in milliseconds)Ü¨␀␀␀␀ÄÇHow long without a message before disconnecting (in milliseconds)Ü¨␀␀␀␀Äídisables nagle algorithm. lowers CPU% and latency but increases bandwidthÜ¨␀␀â¨␀␀␀␀Å^Requires wss connections on server, only to be used with SSL cert.json, never with reverse proxy.
